--- A(i) LEMMA HE6-0'' carries BOTH consumed clauses -------------------------
Span HE6_PROOF_2026-08-08.md:215-238 (delimiters verified §B). Read in full.

Consumption site 1, S1.2 (SLOT-V): d(A(xi)) = h(A), with h the level-one
dv-minimum bound by r2 repair 7 as dv(sum_j a_j x^j) = min_j{e1 v(a_j)+jh}.
Source, line 218: "dv(A(ξ)) = min_i(e₁v(a_i) + ih) EXACTLY". MATCH, at
"ANY point ξ of K̄₀ satisfying (T1) and (T2)" (line 217) = the instance's Pt.
Domain matches too: source "Let A = Σ_{i<D′}a_ix^i with a_i ∈ O",
master "for every nonzero A ∈ O[x] with deg A < D".

Consumption site 2, S1.2 (HE6-SEAM) and S3.2's restatement:
  res(A(xi)/varpi(xi)^k) = iota_xi(gamma_k(A)) * eta_xi^{-q(k)}.
Source, lines 219-221: "the residue of the attaining class, read after division
by ϖ(ξ)^{dv(A)}, is ι_ξ(γ)·η_ξ^{−q} **[r2 sign corrected, PE2 F-3: dividing by
ϖ^k instead of n(k) MULTIPLIES the n(k)-read residue by res(n(k)/ϖ^k) = η^{−q};
the [r1] text read +q]**". MATCH including the minus sign, and the bracket's
res(n(k)/ϖ^k) = η^{−q} is byte-for-content the master's (Q-DEF).

Internal consistency check I ran on the master's own two displays:
  res(A/varpi^k) = res(A/n(k)) * res(n(k)/varpi^k)
                 = iota(dig A) * eta^{-q(k)}   by (SLOT-R) and (Q-DEF).
So (SLOT-R)+(Q-DEF) => (HE6-SEAM) exactly, with dig = gamma_k. Consistent; no
sign seam. Cross-check against the source RIDER (HE6:170-175,
"ϖ(θ)^k/n(k)(θ) = (θ^{e₁}π^{−h})^{q} = η_θ^{q}") also agrees.

Sign of q re-derived independently at the source's own witness (HE6:225-227,
(e1,f1,h)=(2,2,3), k=3, A=x): gamma=1, q(3)=1, so (HE6-SEAM) predicts
eta^{-1}=2eta; source records "the ϖ-read realizes η^{−1} = 2η (PE2's CXRES),
where the [r1] +q reading predicts η". Master's sign is the corrected one.

Coefficient-normalizer seam (r4 repair 9's disclosure), re-derived by me:
the source's gamma is the BARE sum "γ = Σ_t res(a_{i₀+e₁t})η_θ^{t}" (HE6:222-223)
while (GAMMA) carries pi^{-(k-(i+e1 t)h)/e1}. I re-ran HE3-1L's proof arithmetic
(HE3:519-527) rather than trusting the note:
    c_i θ^{i₀+e₁t} / n(κ)(θ)  with n(κ)=x^{i₀}π^{(κ−i₀h)/e₁}
      = c_i · θ^{e₁t} · π^{−(κ−i₀h)/e₁}
      = [c_i π^{−v(c_i)}] · (θ^{e₁}π^{−h})^t     since (κ−i₀h)/e₁ = v(c_i)+th,
so the residue is res(c_i π^{−(κ−(i₀+e₁t)h)/e₁})·η_θ^t — the height-NORMALIZED
coefficient, exactly (GAMMA)'s summand. Repair 9's reading is forced, and its
forcing argument is correct: with the literal bare reading a slot with
v(c_i)>0 contributes 0, contradicting the source's own "the coefficients
ranging over F_Q freely and independently" (HE3:527-528). CLEAN.
Also checked: (k − (i+e1 t)h)/e1 is an integer for every summand of (GAMMA)
(since ih ≡ k mod e1 and (i+e1 t)h ≡ ih), and slots above height k give
positive pi-valuation hence residue 0 — the master's "Terms strictly above
height k contribute zero" is then a theorem, not an extra hypothesis.

